The Qwen3 ordered BF16 normalization/RoPE and explicit-state decoder-block
composition derive from target 6d60bf84c949a0f1310f58007f25d206266f41cd.
The mixed W8 selection, scoped affine quantization, tied quantized table and
Q/K normalization-to-RoPE kernel derive from EngineTailor source
45664def85c5b108239a7ab0d69ba6da34916812, preserving the OMoE experiment lineage.
MiniCPM5 ordered BF16 execution, packed residual RMSNorm and whole-step
compilation derive from target 1dc682fcde3a80cd6917d0b06d124a79caa112aa.
MiniCPM5 tapped verification, padded independent M1 projections and DSpark
integration derive from target df20140e26ea1ef0951747fa192a3891afa24845.
These revisions describe provenance, not qualification of the ApxInf port.

The Clef g20 per-call FP16 Q4 decode, row padding and four-value gated delta
recurrence kernels derive from EngineTailor
feat/clef-g20-engine 6edc065c6ffd12bc347e5d06d77b5a000eb87e9d.
The Clef C14 row decode, Steel-loop and wm1/wn2 split FP16 GEMMs, gate GEMM with
SwiGLU epilogue, causal depthwise convolution and eight-lane gated delta
recurrence kernels derive from EngineTailor campaign/clef-flash9b-m1pro
4030047b, frontier source SHA-256
235c37b2f6a9b365b7898fed6df5a98ff37935c7b06e7f5e24c0afa67463c66d.

The gated delta recurrence and the half-split rotary embedding kernel adapt
MLX-VLM 0.7.4, revision 00093678a1f6bd513212d94778ffc381d6d731bf.
Copyright (c) 2025 Prince Canuma. MIT License.

